{"generated_at":"2026-10-18T01:06:52+00:00","season":2026,"home_field_advantage":2.51,"home_scoring_bump":3.88,"league_avg_points":26.2,"games_final":488,"games_upcoming":81,"settings":{"_comment":"Every knob in the model. Edit this file, commit, and the next run recalculates everything. This is the web version of the workbook's Settings sheet.","season":2026,"prior_season":2025,"currency":"CAD","currency_symbol":"C$","timezone":"America/Toronto","tiers":{"_note":"Tier input is compressed expected return per unit at the offered price, capped by no-vig model value, minus selection and confidence reserves. Probability edge is published separately. Version 2026-09-06-ev2; historical tiers stay frozen.","best_bet":0.07,"good":0.045,"lean":0.025},"model":{"projection_blend":0.5,"_projection_blend_note":"Fraction of the model's disagreement with the posted line that survives into the actionable projection. College markets are softer than the NFL, so half survives, but the market remains the scale anchor.","max_spread_disagreement":12,"_max_spread_disagreement_note":"Raw spread disagreements are squeezed through a tanh curve before projection_blend is applied. This stops an early-season rating-scale miss from turning a 40-point favourite into a coin flip while preserving ordinary 2-6 point opinions.","total_projection_blend":0.55,"max_total_disagreement":14,"edge_compression":0.095,"_edge_compression_note":"Displayed/actionable probability edge is squeezed through 9.5% * tanh(raw/9.5%). Small edges remain useful; a bogus 20% edge is shown near the ceiling instead of presented as a real 20% advantage. Raw edge remains in the data for auditing.","market_blend":0.5,"_market_blend_note":"Weight given to the de-vigged market probability. Higher = more humble. The market is a consensus of everyone with money on the line; a single rating model should not assume it knows better.","max_model_prob":0.85,"margin_sd":13,"_margin_sd_note":"Kept at 13 on purpose. It converts a projected margin into a win probability, and 13-14 is where that conversion agrees with DraftKings' own moneylines (checked on 330 games). Raising it toward the 14.5 measured against closing spreads would hand every underdog moneyline 1-2 points of fake win probability.","scale_margin_to_market":true,"_scale_margin_to_market_note":"Removes the board-wide straight-line tilt between model margins and posted spreads (fitted on FBS-vs-FBS games each run), keeping only each game's own disagreement. Needed because blowouts are capped at mov_cap, so ratings are squeezed and every big spread otherwise reads as an underdog play. false = use raw ratings.","total_sd":14.5,"_total_sd_note":"How far a final combined score typically lands from the closing total. Measured on 266 completed 2026 games: 14.6 points. The old 10 made every over/under look about a third more certain than it is.","use_key_numbers":true,"home_field_fallback":2.4,"rest_day_weight":0.35,"travel_weight_per_1000mi":0.8,"min_games_for_full_confidence":4,"early_season_shrink":0.55,"_early_season_shrink_note":"How hard to pull a team's current-season rating back toward its preseason prior before it has min_games_for_full_confidence games played.","selection_haircut":0.01,"confidence_penalty_max":0.018,"_confidence_penalty_note":"Bounded expected-return reserve: (1-confidence) \u00d7 1.8%, plus the selection haircut. Confidence never multiplies the tier thresholds.","_selection_haircut_note":"Winner's-curse conservatism, subtracted from every estimated edge before tiering. You only bet where the model disagrees with the market, which is also where the model's own error is largest, so selected edges are overstated even when the model is calibrated across all games -- walk-forward simulation puts that gap at 9-15 points of probability. Raise it to bet less and more selectively. Re-measure with `python -m pipeline.backtest` on your own data rather than trusting this number.","_market_blend_calibration_note":"0.50 was chosen because it minimised out-of-sample calibration error in walk-forward simulation across both a sharp market and a soft one (mean absolute gap 0.045-0.050 at 0.50, vs 0.049-0.073 at 0.35 and 0.055-0.058 at 0.65). Profitability in simulation depends entirely on how inefficient you assume the market is, so it was not used to pick this value."},"ratings":{"use_prior_season":false,"_use_prior_season_note":"Off: 2025 results are not used anywhere. Ratings start from ESPN's current 2026 FPI (updated weekly with this season's games) and move with 2026 results. Leak-free test on 2026 week 3 (ratings frozen before the lines opened): DraftKings' spread moved toward this model from open to close 69% of the time (n=32) and the total 67% (n=38), versus 61%/72% with 2025 blended in, and margin error was lower. true = blend last season back in.","ridge_lambda":18,"current_season_prior_strength":10,"_current_season_prior_strength_note":"Weight kept on the 2026 FPI prior as 2026 results come in, in team-games of evidence. 10 had the lowest margin and totals error in the week 2-3 walk-forward (6 and 3 were close; 3 was worse).","mov_cap":28,"recency_halflife_games":14,"prior_season_weight":0.35,"_prior_season_weight_note":"How much last season's solved ratings carry into this season's preseason prior (regression to the mean).","prior_regression":0.62,"_prior_regression_note":"Fraction of last season's rating retained as the preseason prior. 0.62 ~ typical year-over-year correlation in CFB.","fpi_weight":1.0,"_fpi_weight_note":"Share of the preseason margin prior taken from current-season ESPN FPI. 1.0 = FPI only (2025 is off; see use_prior_season).","fpi_scoring_weight":1.0,"_fpi_scoring_weight_note":"Share of the totals prior taken from 2026 FPI offense/defense/special-teams. 1.0 = FPI only; 2025 scoring is not used. 2026 results then take over at current_season_prior_strength.","scoring_prior_games":40,"home_scoring_prior_games":120,"_recency_note":"Half-life in team-games (x7 = days). 14 means a game from ~3 months ago counts half as much as this week's."},"markets":{"moneyline":true,"spread":true,"total":true},"filters":{"_note":"Bets that fail these are shown but never auto-logged to the ledger.","preferred_min_price":-350,"preferred_max_price":500,"_preferred_price_note":"Prices outside this preferred band may still qualify, but are capped at LEAN and staked at half size.","min_price":-600,"max_price":1000,"_hard_price_note":"Absolute pricing stop. Rows beyond this range stay visible as AVOID; they are never logged or staked.","skip_if_no_odds":true,"max_bets_per_game":1,"_max_bets_per_game_note":"Correlation guard. 1 means the model picks only its single best angle on a game (ML and ATS on the same team are ~the same bet).","exclude_fcs_opponents":true,"soft_spread_projection_gap":10,"soft_total_projection_gap":10,"soft_raw_market_prob_gap":0.22,"_soft_guard_note":"Crossing a soft rail caps the play at LEAN and reduces stake rather than deleting it from the actionable middle of the board.","max_spread_projection_gap":18,"_max_spread_projection_gap_note":"Hard spread blind-spot stop. Moderate disagreements are handled by the soft rail first.","max_total_projection_gap":18,"_max_total_projection_gap_note":"Hard total blind-spot stop.","guard_headroom":1.35,"_guard_headroom_note":"A safety rail must never sit below the bar it is protecting. Edge rises with the raw model/market gap, so a confidence-scaled tier threshold is itself a minimum raw gap in disguise; if the ceiling below lands under that minimum, the two guards overlap to zero and NOTHING can qualify at any price. That is exactly what silenced the entire 2026 opening slate. This widens the ceiling, only when it has to, to sit 35% above whatever a LEAN currently requires. Set to 1.0 to disable and apply the ceilings literally.","max_raw_market_prob_gap":0.4,"_max_raw_market_prob_gap_note":"Hard rejection for truly extreme disagreements before market blending can hide a ratings failure.","thin_data_confidence_threshold":0.5,"soft_thin_data_spread_gap":8,"soft_thin_data_total_gap":8,"soft_thin_data_raw_market_prob_gap":0.18,"max_thin_data_spread_gap":14,"max_thin_data_raw_market_prob_gap":0.32,"_thin_data_guard_note":"Before both teams have meaningful current-season data, moderate gaps are LEAN-only at reduced stake; only genuinely extreme gaps are rejected.","max_plays_per_week":10,"_max_plays_per_week_note":"Hard cap on how many bets the model logs in a calendar week, best edges first. Without it a loose threshold plus a full Saturday slate will happily stake 60 bets."},"data":{"espn_group":80,"_espn_group_note":"80 = FBS (I-A). Use 81 for FCS.","odds_provider_priority":["DraftKings","ESPN BET","Caesars Sportsbook","consensus","numberfire","teamrankings"],"lookahead_days":10,"lookback_days":5,"odds_book":"DraftKings","_odds_book_note":"Every play is priced off this one book's line. ESPN's keyless feed carries one sportsbook per game (DraftKings), so no second market is required or checked. If a game has no DraftKings quote, the single best posted line is used instead."},"timing":{"full_tier_min_hours":0,"late_stake_multiplier":0.6,"_note":"Plays priced less than this many hours before kickoff are capped at LEAN. Walk-forward on 2026 weeks 3-4: ATS on 4+ pt disagreements was 54% at 120h+, falling to 44-48% inside 72h, and the line moved toward the model by +0.92 pts early vs +0.18 near kickoff. GOOD/BEST picks made in the early window are locked in state/early_plays.json and graded at their locked price. Set 0 to disable."}},"brier":null,"odds_health":{"healthy":true,"games_checked":81,"games_with_verified_prices":15,"markets":{"ML":15,"ATS":10,"TOTAL":11},"price_observations":72,"unique_prices":34,"flat_price_warning":false,"message":"Only complete two-sided sportsbook prices are actionable."},"quote_coverage":{"provider_checks":48,"books":["Draft Kings"],"odds_book":"DraftKings","games_on_book":10,"games_priced":10,"status":"single-book","note"